# localized-context-needles.txt — operator-instance PII needle list (TEMPLATE)
#
# Purpose:
#   Fixed-string "needles" that the PII pre-commit guard (core/hooks/git-pre-commit-pii.sh),
#   the scope-segregation guardrail (core/hooks/block-scope-segregation.sh, #384),
#   and deploy.sh Check 25 (universal-vs-localized-context) match against staged
#   additions / the tracked corpus / outbound tracker filings to keep ORGANIZATIONAL
#   IDENTITY and PRIVATE-PROJECT CONTENT out of public destinations: coworker names,
#   the employer / org name, the org's email domain, AND (per #384 CD-4) client
#   names, project codes, and internal-system names. These literals are intentionally
#   NOT baked into the tracked hook or detector — a hardcoded employer domain in a
#   public regex is itself a published leak — so they live here, in a gitignored
#   operator-instance file.
#
# How it is used:
#   This is the .example TEMPLATE (tracked, public-safe, ZERO real names).
#   install.sh / update.sh / setup-workspace.sh copy it to the operator-instance
#   dir as `localized-context-needles.txt` ONLY IF that file does not yet exist
#   (create-once — your real list is never overwritten on update). The resolved
#   path is owned by core/deploy/lib-instance-path.sh (pmo_localized_needles);
#   default <instance-dir>/localized-context-needles.txt, override via
#   PMO_LOCALIZED_NEEDLES.
#
# Format:
#   - One needle per line.
#   - Lines beginning with `#` are comments; blank lines are ignored.
#   - Matching is FIXED-STRING (grep -F), case-insensitive — no regex, no escaping.
#   - Keep each needle specific enough to avoid false positives on common words.
#
# Fail-closed note:
#   While this file holds ONLY commented placeholder rows (as shipped), it counts
#   as "unfilled". If your operator-instance dir exists but this file is missing
#   or unfilled, the pre-commit guard fails closed (once its .mode is flipped to
#   enforce) so the organizational-identity tier can never silently no-op. Replace
#   the placeholder rows below with your real needles to activate scanning.
#
# Replace the example rows below (delete the leading `# ` and edit) — do NOT
# commit real names to the repo; this file is gitignored at the instance dir.

# --- Coworker / collaborator names (one per line) ---
# Jane Q. Example
# John Doe

# --- Employer / organization name(s) ---
# Example Corporation
# ExampleCorp

# --- Organization email / web domain(s) ---
# examplecorp.com
# example.org

# --- Client / project-code / internal-system names (private-project content, #384 CD-4) ---
# Names that identify a private engagement and must never reach a scope:public
# tracker destination. Consumed by the scope-segregation guardrail
# (core/hooks/block-scope-segregation.sh) when filing to a scope:public tracker.
# One needle per line; keep each specific enough to avoid false positives.
# Acme Cutover
# PROJ-1234
# internal-billing-system
